WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.320
A light shines above a metal table, with a
chair positioned on either side.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.720
This is the isolated, hermetically-sealed
interview chamber of Provisional Site 23.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.559
Outside the room waits two shell-shocked human
Mobile Task Force members, another with invisible

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:18.949
ghost legs, three powerful cyborgs, and a
scientist from another dimension.

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:24.140
They’re all here to talk about one thing:
The nightmare that unfolded at Site 13, also

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.819
known as SCP - 1730.

00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:31.479
Everyone thinks they know the story: A mysterious
site suddenly appears in Texas, seeming to

00:00:31.479 --> 00:00:36.100
exactly match the blueprint for an abandoned
site that’s supposed to be in Nome, Alaska.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.250
What started as a simple anomalous location
turned out to be an epic horror from another

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:41.250
dimension.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:46.030
The task forces sent in by the Foundation
were either massacred or trapped inside, and

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:50.610
those who survived reported seeing unspeakable
carnage inside the base including a death

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.219
machine designed to destroy anomalies.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:57.809
And that’s not all - as a result of the
mysterious Thresher machine, the entire location

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:02.339
had been transformed into a shifting, spatial
anomaly filled with creatures straight out

00:01:02.339 --> 00:01:07.760
of a nightmare - from giant, telepathic leech
monsters, to huge, multi-limbed Demi Gods

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.940
that would eternally punish the site’s murderous
director, Elliot Emerson.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.000
It was only through the combined might of
three different Mobile Task Forces - including

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.210
the legendary Samsara - and the sacrifice
of brave Captain Hollis that this cursed location

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:26.090
was finally flung into a different dimension,
neutralizing the threat it posed to our reality.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:30.500
But for the SCP Foundation, the story doesn’t
end with neutralization - there’s still

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.500
plenty more questions that need answering.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.640
That’s why, today, we’re going to tell
you what they found out after the neutralization

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.560
of SCP - 1730.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.730
Not only will we discover what’s become
of the many people involved, we learn about

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:46.640
what happened in the last moments before the
neutralization took place.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.710
And perhaps most importantly of all, for the
sake of our universe, we will find out how

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.920
Site 13 came into existence - and how Site
Director Emerson went down such a dark path.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.030
It’s time to get some answers.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:03.000
Welcome to the final part of the SCP - 1730
Saga, as we close the book on one of the most

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.140
deadly locations in the Foundation multiverse.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:10.450
First to sit down in the interview chair was
Captain Ephram Ross, leader of Mobile Task

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.420
Force Apollo 3 also known as The Game Wardens.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:18.120
He was a shaken man, looking far older than
his 35 years, his eyes heavy with the weight

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.280
of the horrors he’d seen.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.830
He and his team were among the first to venture
into the bowels of Site 13 and witness the

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:28.620
atrocities that’d gone on down there like
the Body Pit, full of fleshy slurry, or the

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.390
countless containment chambers that marked
their occupants for vivisection and termination.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:37.420
Captain Ross was haunted by the things that
had happened to his team under his watch such

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.840
as the anomalous transformation of Houston’s
legs and the nightmarish warping death of

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.410
Noah at the hands of a stretchy, reality-bending
anomaly.

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.470
He compared the state of chaos going on down
there to something like Jurassic Park, where

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.890
all hell had broken loose and the monsters
ruled.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:56.700
He also remarked on the Olympia Containment
Cells, each the size of a football stadium,

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.250
capable of containing things far beyond the
scope of this universe’s SCP Foundation.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:05.640
His interviewer was the hard-nosed Dr. Peter
Vincent, who thanked Captain Ross for his

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:10.069
contributions, and called in the next interview
subject: Agent Liam Ohalo, a Game Wardens

00:03:10.069 --> 00:03:12.840
Task Force member working under Captain Ross.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.420
He had a thousand yard stare, and even the
untrained observer could see that Agent Ohalo

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.950
had left some part of himself back in Site
13.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:24.620
When Dr. Vincent attempted to interview him,
he mostly remained silent, only volunteering

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:25.860
one grim sentiment:

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.370
“We should’ve died in there.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:28.370
This isn’t real.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.370
This isn’t real.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.400
We were supposed to die in there.”

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:36.170
Next to be interviewed was Captain Irantu
of Mobile Task Force Tau-5, aka Samsara.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:40.400
His interviewer, Dr. Isha Saint Claire, questioned
him about the nature of the mission, and the

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.870
cybernetic soldier was even-keeled about the
matter.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:47.130
He said that, in spite of regrettable losses
of life, he was still satisfied with the outcome

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.430
of the mission overall.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:53.460
The high-value targets were rescued, the anomaly
was - for all intents and purposes - neutralized,

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.040
and the degree of loss was actually better
than their pre-mission predictions.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.610
It seems that the weight of death doesn’t
weigh quite as heavily on those who will probably

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:05.099
never have to experience it, as the Samsara
team are capable of simply being rebooted

00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:07.980
into new bodies if terminated in the field.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.069
People like Captain Hollis weren’t as lucky.

00:04:10.069 --> 00:04:14.440
Next, Agent Cotter Houston of the Game Wardens
was both interviewed and medically evaluated

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.800
by Dr. Ian Harris.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:20.269
Agent Houston had his legs dematerialized
after he tripped into a rising tide of anomalous

00:04:20.269 --> 00:04:24.159
liquids - which he described as looking like
a moving, physical computer glitch.

00:04:24.159 --> 00:04:28.419
However, in spite of this, Agent Houston is
still able to stand and move of his own free

00:04:28.419 --> 00:04:29.419
will.

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:33.059
It seemed to Dr. Harris that Houston’s legs
were somehow trapped between dimensions.

00:04:33.059 --> 00:04:37.659
Houston told Dr. Harris that he didn’t experience
any kind of pain when his legs were removed,

00:04:37.659 --> 00:04:41.509
but to this day, he occasionally feels something
furry brushing up against them.

00:04:41.509 --> 00:04:43.520
Perhaps, wherever his legs are, they aren’t
alone...

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:49.020
Next, the stoic Agent Munru of Samsara was
interviewed by Captain Elliott O’Neil of

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:52.540
Mobile Task Force D-26, also known as Time
Cops.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:56.449
Captain O’Neil had a bone to pick with Munru
- namely, that he’d allowed Captain Hollis

00:04:56.449 --> 00:05:01.139
to run off and sacrifice her own life, despite
having a clear directive to prevent the human

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:04.580
task force members from endangering themselves
at any cost.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:08.189
Munru deflected, claiming that when Hollis
separated from the group, he assumed that

00:05:08.189 --> 00:05:11.389
she ran off with intentions that never included
her own demise.

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:15.699
O’Neil and the Foundation found this answer
unsatisfying, and decided to move on to their

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:20.009
next interview with Onru - the last person
with Captain Hollis before her death.

00:05:20.009 --> 00:05:24.249
The interviewer, Dr. Darian Arnold, probed
the elite Samsara operative on why she turned

00:05:24.249 --> 00:05:28.779
off her camera before she and Hollis reached
the Thresher - the machine that Hollis overloaded

00:05:28.779 --> 00:05:31.310
to annihilate Site 13 from our dimension.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:35.249
She gave a more compelling answer than Munru:
When she and Hollis entered a server room

00:05:35.249 --> 00:05:39.259
on the way to the Thresher, they encountered
what may have been the ultimate cognitohazard:

00:05:39.259 --> 00:05:43.300
It was a vision of a terrifying alternate
dimension with billions dead.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:47.229
A poisoned star like the biblical wormwood
fell from the burning sky.

00:05:47.229 --> 00:05:52.069
A Nightmare God, like the one torturing Elliot
Emerson, wandered among fields of crucified

00:05:52.069 --> 00:05:55.080
people, covered in deadly, cognitohazardous
runes.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:59.830
Just looking at it burned the SCRAMBLE technology
out of Munru’s eyes, and she turned off

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:03.430
her cameras to avoid potentially frying the
brains of mission control.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.169
Hollis wasn’t so lucky.

00:06:05.169 --> 00:06:09.119
The things she witnessed broke her sanity,
and when she finally overloaded the Thresher

00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:11.089
machine, she was laughing and crying.

00:06:11.089 --> 00:06:15.319
Finally, in perhaps the most enlightening
debriefing interview of them all, Site Director

00:06:15.319 --> 00:06:19.669
Willam Vesterland interviewed Dr. Mohammed
Scott - The highest-ranking researcher of

00:06:19.669 --> 00:06:24.289
Site 13, and confidant of the now-infamous
Director Elliot Emerson.

00:06:24.289 --> 00:06:28.349
The question was simple: just what had happened
for Site 13 to become so messed up?

00:06:28.349 --> 00:06:33.240
And Dr. Scott answered in detail, with a tale
of corruption, alternate realities, and the

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.219
perils of unchecked power.

00:06:35.219 --> 00:06:39.599
In his home dimension, Site 13 was originally
created in Nome, Alaska to house the corpse

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:44.430
of a giant sea creature that beached itself
on the border of India and Bangladesh in 1964.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:49.089
It became the largest and most secretive Foundation
containment facility in the latter half of

00:06:49.089 --> 00:06:50.240
the 20th century.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:56.060
However, disaster struck in 1994, when a Marxist
extremist used an anomaly to level the Willis

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.449
Tower in Chicago.

00:06:57.449 --> 00:07:01.559
As a result, the Foundation lost a lot of
its funding and international support, leaving

00:07:01.559 --> 00:07:03.530
it in dire financial straits.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:07.680
Enter the true villain of the Site 13 story:
Paul Manafort.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:11.789
If that name sounds familiar to you, it’s
because he was an associate of President Trump

00:07:11.789 --> 00:07:15.650
in our universe who got into legal trouble
for shady international dealings.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:19.729
However, in Dr. Scott’s universe, he was
a powerful staffer for President Bob Dole

00:07:19.729 --> 00:07:24.820
- who in that reality had beaten Bill Clinton
in the 1996 Presidential Election.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:29.599
Manafort was made the new Secretary General
of the Global Occult Coalition - The UN’s

00:07:29.599 --> 00:07:34.180
answer to the SCP Foundation, and one of their
leading competitors, with an ethos geared

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:40.159
towards killing rather than containing anomalies.Manafort
and the GOC co-opted the struggling Foundation,

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:42.539
providing them with money in exchange for
control.

00:07:42.539 --> 00:07:45.529
The Foundation had no choice but to accept
this deal with the devil.

00:07:45.529 --> 00:07:49.530
Slowly, Manafort replaced the Foundation old
guard with toadies and loyalists.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.479
The Ethics Committee and the O5 command were
dismantled.

00:07:52.479 --> 00:07:56.550
Dissenters were dragged out of their offices
and shot point blank in the head, execution-style.

00:07:56.550 --> 00:08:02.069
Site 13 had originally been directed by Dr.
Bright, but Bright was arrested and contained

00:08:02.069 --> 00:08:06.860
under false pretences so Manafort could install
a new director: A mid-level researcher by

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.439
the name of Elliot Emerson.

00:08:08.439 --> 00:08:13.259
Emerson is often painted as a sadistic monster
who took pleasure in torturing anomalies to

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:15.699
death and flushing them down the body pit.

00:08:15.699 --> 00:08:21.069
The reality is both simpler and more grim:
Emerson, it turns out, was just an eager yes

00:08:21.069 --> 00:08:22.069
man.

00:08:22.069 --> 00:08:25.990
He was put into his position to follow Manafort’s
orders to a tee, and those orders were simple

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:26.990
- Kill.

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:31.749
In a perfect example of the banality of evil,
Director Emerson converted Site 13 into a

00:08:31.749 --> 00:08:35.849
brutal slaughterhouse, just as his overlords
at the GOC had ordered him.

00:08:35.849 --> 00:08:39.371
But things were quickly getting out of hand,
and one of the most vocal critics of the new

00:08:39.371 --> 00:08:44.440
regime was one of Emerson’s old lovers,
one Dr. Vera Hadley, Assistant Director of

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.730
Anomalous Biology.

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:50.730
Dr. Hadley was disgusted by the inhuman acts
Emerson was carrying out and couldn’t stay

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:54.149
silent, and for this she faced horrific consequences.

00:08:54.149 --> 00:08:57.640
Corrupt guards stripped her and beat her to
within an inch of her life in front of her

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:58.640
co-workers.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:00.620
In that moment, she swore her revenge.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.660
She sabotaged the containment procedures and
had the engineers rig the already unstable

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.430
Thresher device to overload.

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:11.100
As Emerson watched the anomalies break containment
he began to fear for his life - both from

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:15.340
the anomalies themselves, and from the punishments
of his superiors at the GOC.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:18.810
Dr. Scott revealed that Emerson was no evil
mastermind.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.510
He was a lapdog for the GOC.

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.160
A dirty coward, all the way to the very end.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.450
And he was desperate.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:28.860
He held Dr. Scott at gunpoint and ordered
him to activate the Thresher or die, and the

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:29.970
rest is history.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:33.970
There would be no redemption for Dr. Scott’s
former friend, as Emerson ended up chained

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:38.350
to the rune-covered, platform head of a Nightmare
God for all eternity.

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:43.420
So ends the debriefing of the Site 13 survivors,
and closes the book on that terrible place

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:44.750
- for now, anyway.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:49.790
The story of SCP - 1730 is anything but simple,
and there are so many angles from which this

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:53.120
dark tragedy of cruelty and corruption can
be approached.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:57.600
And ultimately, it was all for the same two
things at the root of every evil: The desire

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.350
for money and power.

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:03.940
But the pursuit of these base desires can
lead to some truly nightmarish consequences,

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:08.120
and nobody knows this better than former Director
Elliot Emerson - who’ll be paying for these

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:11.660
sins until the end of time, and perhaps even
beyond.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:16.730
Now go check out another epic tale from the
SCP Foundation, SCP-5000 - The Suit.

